02:23:55,296 --> 02:24:00,256
这就是语言模型在实际应用中，它能很好地理解语言。
So this is the language model in action and it understands the language very well.

1748
02:24:00,462 --> 02:24:04,576
无论我们给它什么，它都能理解并给出答案。
Whatever we are giving it, it is able to understand and give us the answer.

1749
02:24:04,736 --> 02:24:05,056
好的。
Okay.

1750
02:24:05,998 --> 02:24:16,016
智能体之所以能执行所有这些任务，是因为它们利用了语言模型，因为这些模型能够理解语言或文本，
So agents can perform all these tasks by using the language model because the models are able to understand the language or text,

1751
02:24:16,176 --> 02:24:24,736
对吧？所以智能体应该能够带我们从一个地方到另一个地方，而智能体提供的价值是，
right? So agent should be able to take us from one place to another, and the value that the agent is adding,

1752
02:24:24,976 --> 02:24:33,220
智能体有能力访问外部世界或工具，并且能够做出决策并制定计划。
agent is capable of accessing the external world or tools and be able to make decisions and come up with a plan.

1753
02:24:33,456 --> 02:24:40,740
一个智能体应该有记忆，并且能够听取人类的反馈并纠正任何错误。
An agent should have a memory and an agent be able to listen to the human feedback and rectify any mistakes.

1754
02:24:41,038 --> 02:24:43,492
这就是智能体的定义。
So that is the definition of an agent.

1755
02:24:43,982 --> 02:24:45,860
所以不用担心这些理论。
So don't worry about the theory.

1756
02:24:46,176 --> 02:24:50,176
一旦我们构建起项目，你就会理解所有这些概念了，对吧？
Once we build a project, then you will understand all these concepts, right?

1757
02:24:50,496 --> 02:24:59,136
在接下来的课程中，我们将深入探讨语言模型，但我希望通过这些例子，你已经对什么是智能体有了很好的理解。
So we will deep dive into the language models in the coming lectures, but I hope with these examples you got a pretty good understanding on what an agent is.

1758
02:24:59,538 --> 02:25:00,644
好的，谢谢大家。
All right, Thank you.

1759
02:25:01,134 --> 02:25:05,092
让我们学习关于智能体的另一个主题：代理水平。
Let's learn one other topic with the agents that is level of agency.

1760
02:25:05,536 --> 02:25:10,084
那么，一个智能体应该具备多少程度的代理水平？
So, how much level of agency does an agent should have?

1761
02:25:10,256 --> 02:25:15,716
也就是说，一个智能体拥有的控制权或自主性被称为代理水平。
That is, the level of control or autonomy an agent has is called agency.

1762
02:25:16,016 --> 02:25:25,696
也就是说，要将某物视为一个智能体，基本要求是它必须使用 LLM，并且能够使用工具。
That is, in order to consider something as an agent, the basic requirement is it should use the LLM and also be able to use the tools.

1763
02:25:25,966 --> 02:25:29,376
例如，让我们去 ChatGPT。
For example, let's go to ChatGPT.

1764
02:25:29,774 --> 02:25:31,216
我们来提个问题。
So let's ask a question.

1765
02:25:31,502 --> 02:25:34,020
列出纽约最值得游览的 10 个地方。
List the top 10 places to visit in New York.

1766
02:25:34,958 --> 02:25:35,216
对吧？
Right?

1767
02:25:35,406 --> 02:25:39,776
如果你注意到这里，ChatGPT 正在尝试进行网络搜索。
And if you notice here, ChatGPT is trying to do the web search.

1768
02:25:40,976 --> 02:25:41,296
好的。
Okay.

1769
02:25:42,766 --> 02:25:46,112
这意味着它正在使用一个网络搜索工具，对吧？
So that means it is using a web search tool, right?

1770
02:25:46,272 --> 02:25:51,472
所以这是一个利用工具来提供结果的 LLM，也就是 Chat GPT。
So it's an LLM that is Chat GPT using a tool to give us the results.

1771
02:25:51,758 --> 02:26:03,552
但在这种情况下，我们并没有进行任何决策或规划，对吧？根据我们对智能体的定义。所以你能理解这个例子中的自主性水平非常低，对吧？
But in this case, we are not taking any decision or planning though, right? As per our definition of an agent. So you understand the level of agency in this example is very minimal, right?

1772
02:26:03,952 --> 02:26:09,312
也就是说，LLM只是调用了网络搜索工具，然后把结果给到我们，对吧？
So the LLM is just using the web search tool, then it is giving us the results, right?

1773
02:26:09,582 --> 02:26:14,912
让我再带你过几个例子，让你理解“自主性”的含义，好吗？
So let me walk you through a few more examples so you understand the meaning of agency, right?

1774
02:26:15,086 --> 02:26:21,792
例如，我们来看这个简单的处理器场景，对吧？也就是一个可以重写句子的语法检查器。
So for example, let's take this scenario simple processor, right? That is grammar checker, which can rewrite a sentence.

1775
02:26:21,966 --> 02:26:32,752
在这种情况下，自主性等级是 1，因为智能体不会影响下一步的操作，对吧？它做的只是检查语法并重写句子，没别的。
In this case, the agency level is one because agent doesn't influence what the next action is, right? All it is doing is just checking the grammar and then rewriting the sentence, nothing else.

1776
02:26:32,912 --> 02:26:40,672
如果你看路由器的案例，比如客户支持查询或聊天机器人，对吧？在这种情况下，智能体决定基础的控制流，对吧？
And if you take the router case, customer support query or chart bot, right? So agent determines basic control flow, right?

1777
02:26:40,846 --> 02:26:42,112
然后给他们答案。
And then give them the answer.

1778
02:26:42,286 --> 02:26:47,492
所以它是在执行一个流程。在这种情况下，自主性等级是 2。
So it is kind of executing a flow. So in this case, the agency level is 2.

1779
02:26:48,078 --> 02:26:50,532
再看另一个场景：工具调用者。
And if you take another scenario, tool caller.

1780
02:26:50,912 --> 02:27:00,672
例如，你有一个智能日历，它能识别“周一见”这样的内容。这就是一段文本，一旦它找到这段文字，就应该安排一次会议，对吧？
For example, you have a smart calendar that checks for let's meet on Monday. So this is the text, and once it finds this text, then it should schedule a meeting, right?

1781
02:27:00,912 --> 02:27:05,552
在这种情况下，智能体决定函数和执行。
So in this case, the agent determines function and execution.

1782
02:27:05,712 --> 02:27:10,032
所以自主性等级是 3，属于多步骤智能体，对吧？
So the agency level is three and multi-step agent, right?

1783
02:27:10,272 --> 02:27:15,632
个人旅行规划器，可以收集航班、酒店以及旅游景点选项。
Personal travel planner that can gather flight, hotel, and places to visit options.

1784
02:27:15,886 --> 02:27:23,312
在这种情况下，智能体制定计划并逐步执行，对吧？这就是为什么自主性等级是 4。
In this case, agent prepares a plan and execute it step by step, right? So that's why the agency level is four.

1785
02:27:23,552 --> 02:27:32,832
而多智能体意味着，例如，旅行规划智能体调用预订智能体，然后预订智能体调用邮件智能体，对吧？这就是多智能体。
And multi-agent means, for example, let's say travel planner agent calls booking agent and then booking agent calls email agent, right? So multi-agent.

1786
02:27:32,992 --> 02:27:45,552
一个智能体工作流启动另一个智能体工作流，对吧？在这种情况下，自主性等级是 5。所以自主性水平越低，智能体创造的价值就越低。
One agent workflow starts another agentic workflow, right? So in this case the agency level is five. So the lower the agency level, the lower is the value created by an agent.

1787
02:27:45,792 --> 02:27:49,540
自主性级别越高，智能体创造的价值就越高。
Higher the agency level, the higher is the value created by an agent.

1788
02:27:49,902 --> 02:27:50,192
好的。
Okay.

1789
02:27:50,832 --> 02:27:58,992
在我们已经看到的例子中，预订机票、规划行程并执行不同操作具有更高的
And in our example that we have seen already, that is booking the flight, planning the trip, and executing different actions has more

1790
02:27:59,152 --> 02:28:04,752
自主性等级，因为自主性本质上就是智能体拥有的控制权，对吧？
levels of agency because agency is nothing but the amount of control an agent has, right?

1791
02:28:05,102 --> 02:28:09,952
也就是说，它拥有工具控制权或决策控制权等，对吧？
That is, it has tool control or decision-making control, etc., right?

1792
02:28:10,446 --> 02:28:21,312
而在这个销售示例中，智能体拥有很多层级的自主性，而最高级别的自主性是当一个智能体工作流调用另一个智能体工作流时，
And in this sales example, agents have a lot of levels of agency, and highest level of agency is when one agentic workflow calls another agentic workflow,

1793
02:28:21,472 --> 02:28:29,698
也就是旅行规划智能体调用预订智能体，预订智能体再调用邮件智能体，这就是多智能体。
which is nothing but travel planner agent calling booking agent, and booking agent calls email agent, So this is nothing but multi-agent.

1794
02:28:30,832 --> 02:28:39,392
所以我们了解到，当一个智能体拥有工具访问权限、能够做出决策并执行操作时，
So we understood that when an agent has tool access and an agent can make a decision and an agent can execute an action,

1795
02:28:39,632 --> 02:28:42,244
这些智能体就具有更高的自主性。
then those agents have higher level of agency.

1796
02:28:42,752 --> 02:28:51,632
因此，自主性级别反映了一个智能体能提供的价值，对吧？自主性水平越低，创造的价值就越少。
So agency level speaks about the value that an agent can provide, right? The lower the agency level, the less the value creation.

1797
02:28:51,792 --> 02:28:58,592
这种价值可以是时间或金钱，对吧？也就是节省时间、增加收入或降低成本，对吧？
The value can be either time or money, right? That is saving time and increasing revenue to reduce costs, right?

1798
02:28:58,926 --> 02:29:05,124
现在让我们进一步简化智能体的定义。一个智能体由两个主要部分组成。
Now let's further simplify the definition of an agent. So an agent consists of two main parts.

1799
02:29:05,326 --> 02:29:06,628
第一个是“大脑”。
The first one is brain.

1800
02:29:06,912 --> 02:29:14,820
大脑就是 LLM，也就是大语言模型。我们将在下一节课中详细学习关于大语言模型的内容。
Brain is nothing but the LLM, that is the large language model. So we will learn about large language model in detail in the next lecture.

1801
02:29:15,232 --> 02:29:27,300
还有处理推理和规划。而第二部分是身体，对吧？所谓身体就是让智能体能够执行动作和任务的工具。
And also to handle reasoning and planning. And the second part is body, right? So the body is nothing but the tools which enable the agent to perform the actions and tasks.

1802
02:29:27,728 --> 02:29:28,048
没错。
Right.

1803
02:29:28,128 --> 02:29:33,168
行动可以是调用邮件工具来发送一封邮件，对吧？
The action can be sending an email by accessing the email tool, right?

1804
02:29:33,408 --> 02:29:43,968
所以不要把 LLM 和智能体搞混。对。LLM 不会自动做出任何决策，也不会自行执行任何动作。
So do not get confused between an LLM and an agent. Right. So LLMs do not take any decisions or they do not perform any actions by themselves.

1805
02:29:44,128 --> 02:29:48,368
而且 LLM 也无法与外部环境交互，对吧？
And LLMs cannot interact with the external environments as well, right?

1806
02:29:48,622 --> 02:29:51,876
也就是说，它们不能自主浏览网页。
That is, they cannot browse web pages on their own.

1807
02:29:51,968 --> 02:30:01,220
但智能体可以做所有这些事情，对吧？配备了工具的 LLM 就是一个具有最低自主性的智能体。
But an agent can do all these things, right? So an LLM equipped with tools is nothing but an agent with minimum agency.

1808
02:30:01,408 --> 02:30:06,116
如果我们再加上规划和推理，它就会变成一个聪明的智能体。
And if we add planning and reasoning, then that would become a smart agent.

1809
02:30:06,448 --> 02:30:12,964
而最终阶段是通用人工智能 AGI 和超人工智能 ASI。
And the final stage is artificial general intelligence AGI and artificial superintelligence ASI.

1810
02:30:13,168 --> 02:30:24,128
我们还没达到那个阶段，所以不用担心这个。在开始构建智能体之前，我们首先需要清楚地理解什么是智能体以及什么是 LLM。
We are not there yet, so let's not worry about it. So before we start building an agent, first we need to have a clear understanding on what an agent is and what is an LLM.

1811
02:30:24,288 --> 02:30:33,028
对吧？这就是为什么我们要详细讲解这一课。我还会再举一个例子，让你更好地理解智能体。
Right? So that's why we are covering this lecture in detail. And I will cover one other example so you will get good understanding on agent.

1812
02:30:33,328 --> 02:30:38,128
例如，我们以这个候选人面试流程为例。
So for example, consider this candidate interview process as an example.

1813
02:30:38,288 --> 02:30:42,448
你知道现在很多候选人都在用 Chat GPT 来回答问题，对吧？
You know nowadays candidates are using Chat GPT to answer the questions, right?

1814
02:30:42,670 --> 02:30:52,164
为了避免这种情况，你加入了视频面试环节，使用了这个 Hireflix 系统，候选人必须录制他们对你提问的回答，然后上传。
So to avoid that, you added this video interview process, you are using this Hardflicks where the candidate has to record the answers for the questions you asked and then they have to upload it.

1815
02:30:52,528 --> 02:31:01,328
在这种情况下，智能体的任务是找到候选人存储的视频，然后识别出优秀候选人的列表。
So in this case, the agent task is to find the video stored by the candidates and then identify the list of good candidates.

1816
02:31:01,488 --> 02:31:05,604
好的。在这种情况下，智能体节省了时间和金钱。
Okay. So in this case the agent is saving the time and money.

1817
02:31:05,808 --> 02:31:15,328
比如，假设有 500 名候选人申请这个职位，你必须查看这 500 个人的视频，并对合适的候选人提供见解。
So for example, let's say you have 500 candidates applied to this position and you have to review 500 candidates' videos and provide insights on the right candidates,

1818
02:31:15,488 --> 02:31:18,448
对吧？那么智能体需要哪些工具呢？
right? So what are the tools that the agent needs?

1819
02:31:18,798 --> 02:31:22,208
它应该能够搜索像 Hireflex 这样的网站，对吧？
It should be able to search a website like Hireflex, right?

1820
02:31:22,288 --> 02:31:32,288
就像 Google 搜索一样，然后访问该网站，因为视频都在这个 Hireflex 网站上，接着它需要下载候选人上传的视频。
Just like Google search and then visit the website because the videos are on this Hireflex website, and then it has to download the videos that are uploaded by the candidates

1821
02:31:32,528 --> 02:31:38,768
然后将这些视频转换为转录文本，对吧？因为我们有语音转文本转换工具，对吧？
and then convert the videos into transcripts, right? Because we have speech to text conversion tools, right?

1822
02:31:38,848 --> 02:31:49,568
所以智能体可以将视频转换为转录文本，然后智能体应该能够分析视频的情感，因为现在的模型非常擅长理解语言，对吧？
So agent can convert the videos into transcripts and then agent should be able to analyze the sentiment of the videos because the models are so good in understanding the language, right?

1823
02:31:49,648 --> 02:31:59,808
也就是说，那个能分析转录文本的语言模型，一旦它理解了内容，就应该能够对候选人进行排名，也就是判断候选人是优秀还是平庸。
So the language model that can analyze the transcript, and then once it understood the transcript, then it should be able to rank the candidates, that is whether the candidate is good or bad,

1824
02:31:59,982 --> 02:32:12,128
对吧？这个智能体是在自主做决策吗？是的，因为它在分析视频情感、判断候选人优劣的同时，也在尝试对候选人进行排序。
right? Is this agent making decisions on its own? Yes, because while analyzing the sentiment of the videos, that is the good candidate or bad candidate, it is also trying to rank the candidates.

1825
02:32:12,366 --> 02:32:15,728
那么在这个例子中，我们需要人机协同反馈吗？
So do we need human in the loop feedback in this example?

1826
02:32:15,982 --> 02:32:26,208
比如，假设作为评估者，我想随机评估一些视频并提供反馈，这样智能体就能收到反馈并纠正任何错误，对吧？
For example, let's say as an evaluator, right? I want to randomly evaluate the videos and provide the feedback so that the agent receives the feedback and rectifies any mistakes, right?

1827
02:32:26,368 --> 02:32:28,036
智能体可能会犯错，对吧？
Agents can make mistakes, right?

1828
02:32:28,208 --> 02:32:41,168
因为它可能会把优秀的候选人标记为差的，或者把差的候选人标记为好的，对吧？所以这些反馈需要存储在智能体记忆中，这样智能体就不会再犯同样的错误了，对吧？
Because they can mark a good candidate as a bad or a bad candidate as a good, right? So this feedback needs to be stored in the agentic memory so the agent cannot repeat the same mistake again, right?

1829
02:32:41,328 --> 02:32:50,768
所以我们知道这个应用具有较高的代理水平，因为它利用工具进行网络搜索并下载视频。
So we know this application has a higher level of agency because it uses the tools to do this web search and then download the videos

1830
02:32:51,182 --> 02:32:58,768
然后进行语音转文本转换、理解语言并进行情感分析，对吧？
and then do the speech to text conversion and understand the language and perform the sentiment analysis, right?

1831
02:32:59,054 --> 02:33:08,448
在这种情况下，智能体使用工具、做出决策、执行动作，并且它拥有记忆并接收人类的反馈，
So in this case, the agent uses the tools, takes the decisions, performs the actions, and the agent has memory and it takes the human feedback,

1832
02:33:08,608 --> 02:33:11,140
对吧？所以这不就是所谓的智能体吗。
right? So this is nothing but an agent.

1833
02:33:11,408 --> 02:33:15,968
通过这些例子，我希望你们理解了智能体的价值，对吧？
So with these examples, I hope you understood the value of an agent, right?

1834
02:33:16,366 --> 02:33:23,088
到目前为止我们学到的内容，是关于围绕智能体的炒作以及相关的研究论文，对吧？
So what we learned so far, we learned about hype around the agents and the research papers around the agents hype, right?

1835
02:33:23,342 --> 02:33:27,728
而且我们也通过各种例子构建了智能体的定义。
And we also constructed the definition of an agent with various examples.

1836
02:33:27,968 --> 02:33:31,168
最后，我们了解了代理水平，对吧？
And lastly, we saw level of agency, right?

1837
02:33:31,328 --> 02:33:33,168
这就是关于智能体的所有内容。
So that's all about agents.

1838
02:33:33,408 --> 02:33:44,768
在下一节课中，我们将学习大语言模型，也就是 LLM。在我们开始构建智能体之前，理解什么是智能体以及什么是 LLM 至关重要。
In the next lecture, we will learn about LLMs, that is, large language models. So understanding what is an agent and what is an LLM is crucial before we start building an agent.

1839
02:33:44,928 --> 02:33:50,368
这就是为什么我们试图通过各种例子来详细了解这些概念。
So that is why we are trying to understand the concepts in detail with various examples.

1840
02:33:50,528 --> 02:33:51,876
好的吗？谢谢大家。
Alright? Thank you.

1841
02:33:52,128 --> 02:33:57,328
那么，在本节课中，让我们来学习什么是 LLM，也就是大语言模型。
So, in this lecture, let's learn about what is an LLM, large language model.

1842
02:33:58,286 --> 02:34:03,716
在上一节课中，我们已经了解到智能体由两个主要部分组成。
So, we already learned in the previous lecture that an agent consists of two main parts.

1843
02:34:04,270 --> 02:34:07,108
一个是大脑，另一个是身体。
One is the brain, and the other one is the body.

1844
02:34:07,536 --> 02:34:11,616
大脑就是 LLM，也就是大语言模型。
Brain is nothing but the LLM, that is the large language model.

1845
02:34:11,822 --> 02:34:14,564
LLM 处理推理和规划。
The LLM handles the reasoning and planning.

1846
02:34:15,136 --> 02:34:23,856
下一个是身体。身体就是让智能体能够执行动作和任务的工具。
And the next one is body. Body is nothing but the tools which enable the agent to perform the actions and tasks.

1847
02:34:24,256 --> 02:34:35,652
所以我们知道 LLM 是智能体的核心或基础。因此，在继续构建智能体之前，我们也需要了解 LLM。
So we know LLM is the brain or foundation of an agent. So we need to understand LLMs as well before we proceed with building the agents.

1848
02:34:35,950 --> 02:34:36,336
对。
Right.

1849
02:34:36,576 --> 02:34:45,220
那么让我们通过一个例子从第一原理来理解 LLM，就像我们在上一节课中了解什么是智能体一样。
So let's understand LLMs from the first principle with an example, just like how we understood what is an agent in the previous lecture.

1850
02:34:45,550 --> 02:34:45,924
对。
Right.

1851
02:34:46,256 --> 02:34:52,868
假设你是一个聪明的外星人，你可以访问所有已发布的资料。
So imagine you are a smart alien and you have access to all the materials that are published.

1852
02:34:53,166 --> 02:35:02,176
例如，书籍、博客或任何公开可用的材料，而且你也懂数学，
For example, let's say books or blogs or any material that is publicly available, and you also know the mathematics

1853
02:35:02,336 --> 02:35:03,776
并且你也能思考。
and you also can think.

1854
02:35:04,496 --> 02:35:08,256
但想象一下，你对语言一窍不通，对吧？
But imagine you don't know anything about the language, right?

1855
02:35:08,590 --> 02:35:10,596
现在是你的任务。
So now here is your task.

1856
02:35:10,926 --> 02:35:17,604
假设我给你一个不完整的句子，你的工作是预测下一个词。
Assume I gave you an incomplete sentence and your job is to predict the next word.

1857
02:35:18,254 --> 02:35:23,296
“敏捷的棕色狐狸跳过懒惰的空白”，对吧？
The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy blank, right?

1858
02:35:23,598 --> 02:35:27,776
所以你必须预测下一个词。记住，你并不懂这门语言。
So you have to predict the next word. Remember, you don't know the language.

1859
02:35:28,014 --> 02:35:30,788
那么你认为该如何解决这个问题呢？
So how do you think you can go about solving this issue?

1860
02:35:31,470 --> 02:35:39,776
其中一种可能的方法是查阅所有可用的书籍，并尝试去搜索我们是否真的能找到这个句子。
So some possible ways could be going through all the available books and trying to search if we can actually find this sentence

1861
02:35:40,174 --> 02:35:41,936
在那些书里，对吧？
in those books, right?

1862
02:35:42,254 --> 02:35:53,136
假设这句话在现有的书籍中出现了 100 次。那么我们可能会选择出现频率最高的那个词作为下一个预测词，对吧？
So assume this sentence is present 100 times in the available books. Then we probably would choose the highest probability word that comes next, right?

1863
02:35:53,326 --> 02:35:59,748
也就是出现频率最高的那个词，对吧？所以那将是你的下一个预测词。
That is the word which comes more frequently, right? So that will be your next prediction word.

1864
02:35:59,936 --> 02:36:07,616
所以这就是我们预测下一个词的方法，但我们要如何预测再下一个词呢？
So that's how we may be able to predict the next word, but how will we predict the next to next words, right?

1865
02:36:07,776 --> 02:36:12,964
这就是在预测“再下一个”词时出现的问题。
So that's where the problem arises in predicting the next to next words.

1866
02:36:13,376 --> 02:36:18,656
假设英语中有 40,000 个词汇量。
And assume in English we have 40,000 vocabulary words.

1867
02:36:18,816 --> 02:36:19,136
好的。
Okay.

1868
02:36:19,536 --> 02:36:26,096
那么为了预测那一个下一个词，我们有 40,000 个选项，对吧？
So to predict that one next word, we will have 40,000 options, right?

1869
02:36:26,656 --> 02:36:34,884
而要预测接下来的两个词，也就是两个词，我们将有 40,000 乘以 40,000 个选项，对吧？
And to predict the next two next word, that is two words, we will have 40,000 times 40,000 options, right?

1870
02:36:35,246 --> 02:36:39,812
如果要预测接下来的 20 个词，就是 40,000 乘以 20。
And to predict the next 20 words, 40,000 times 20.

1871
02:36:40,016 --> 02:36:44,228
这些选项的数量甚至超过了宇宙中粒子的数量。
This is more options than the number of particles that we have in the universe.

1872
02:36:44,416 --> 02:36:49,216
