1878
02:37:17,936 --> 02:37:30,816
并且你想计算它到达地面所需的时间。当我们进行多次实验并收集到这些数据后，你认为我们接下来要做什么？
and you want to calculate the time it takes to reach the ground, right? So once we collect this data after performing several experiments, what do you think we will do once we have the data collected?

1879
02:37:31,118 --> 02:37:44,896
我们会尝试在数据中寻找规律，对吧？这意味着我们将试图建立一个模型，来计算物体从塔顶落到地面需要多少时间。
We will try to find the patterns in the data, right? So that means we will try to create a model for how much time the material took to reach the ground from the top of the tower.

1880
02:37:45,136 --> 02:37:51,300
在这种情况下，公式是：t 是时间，h 是高度，g 是重力加速度。
So the equation is in this case t is the time, h is the height, g is the gravity.

1881
02:37:51,696 --> 02:37:54,496
这就是我们推导出这个公式的方法。
So this is how we came up with this equation.

1882
02:37:54,734 --> 02:37:56,416
那么这个模型的作用是什么？
So what will this model do?

1883
02:37:56,576 --> 02:38:03,856
一旦我们将输入发送给这个模型，模型就能为我们提供结果作为输出。
Once we send the input to this model, then the model can get the output as the result for us.

1884
02:38:04,256 --> 02:38:10,016
同样地，让我们回到从给定句子中预测下一个词的例子。
So similarly, let's go back to our next prediction from a given sentence example.

1885
02:38:10,176 --> 02:38:19,108
没错。如果我们将给定的词组作为输入提供给一个模型，目的是预测下一个 token（标记）呢？
Right. So what if we send the given set of words as an input to a model in order to predict the next token,

1886
02:38:19,456 --> 02:38:29,616
对吧？这种以一系列词作为输入并预测下一个 token 的模型被称为语言模型。
right? So a model which takes a sequence of words as an input and predicts the next token is called a language model.

1887
02:38:30,318 --> 02:38:37,252
通过这些内容，我希望你理解了什么是语言模型，我们将在下一节课中深入探讨。
So, with this, I hope you understood what a language model is, and we will deep dive in the next lecture.

1888
02:38:37,618 --> 02:38:38,864
